    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d212">

                <pb facs="0247" n="1081" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1081"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112Sa/16</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Laughlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-06-08T13:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 8, 1918, 1 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 3.17 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>10509. War Trade Board [from Sheldon]:</p>
                <p>No. 748. I am informed that in consequence of an agreement between Germany and
                    Sweden the Germans will grant safe-conduct letters <pb facs="0248" n="1082"
                        xml:id="pg1082"/> to Swedish steamers carrying noncontraband cargoes under
                    the general agreement between Sweden and the Associated Governments and also to
                    those ships proceeding to oversea countries outside the war zone. Swedish
                    authorities request that permission be granted to carry these letters in such
                    cases as vessels chartered for the Belgian Relief. British agree. Please
                    confirm.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Laughlin</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
